\section{July 31, 2026 — TSSE Unified Architecture Notes}

\subsection*{Objective}
Record current understanding and refinements of the unified TSSE architecture and
its interaction with AITFE and related engines.

\subsection*{Context}
Work focused on:
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
  \item Consolidating TSSE into a single unified chapter.
  \item Verifying temporal symmetry and symplectic consistency across all kernels.
  \item Preparing structures suitable for journal submission and monograph use.
\end{itemize}

\subsection*{Key Formal Objects}
\begin{definition}[Global TSSE Hamiltonian]
Let $(q,p)$ be canonical coordinates. The TSSE engine evolves under
\[
H_{\text{TSSE}} = H_{\text{T}} + H_{\text{RPK}} + H_{\text{FK}} + H_{\text{SIK}}
+ H_{\text{VK}} + H_{\text{SK}} + H_{\text{CK}},
\]
where each term corresponds to temporal, relativistic, fusion, invariant, verification,
stability, and control layers.
\end{definition}

\begin{lemma}[Temporal Admissibility]
If each subsystem Hamiltonian $H_i$ commutes with $\mathcal{T}$, then
\[
[\mathcal{T},H_{\text{TSSE}}] = 0.
\]
\end{lemma}

\begin{proof}
Linearity of the commutator:
\[
[\mathcal{T},H_{\text{TSSE}}]
=
\left[\mathcal{T},\sum_i H_i\right]
=
\sum_i [\mathcal{T},H_i]
=
0.
\]
\end{proof}

\subsection*{Engine-Level Reflections}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
  \item TSSE behaves more naturally as a \emph{stack of kernels} than as a single
        monolithic operator.
  \item The unified chapter is mathematically clean, but operationally the layered
        view (Ch.\ 1–12) is still useful for implementation.
  \item Journal form will likely require a reduced kernel set with one or two
        flagship theorems.
\end{itemize}

